cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Photons to Power Laws: an optical photometry pipeline for gamma-ray burst afterglows"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Harishik Dev Singh"
    family-names: "Jamwal"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Harishik/photons-to-power-laws"
abstract: >-
  A Python pipeline that takes raw optical frames of a gamma-ray burst
  afterglow through calibration, source detection, catalog-based photometric
  calibration with colour terms, image subtraction against a deep template,
  empirical-PSF or aperture photometry (with a PSF and kernel that vary across
  full CCD frames), dust-extinction corrections, multi-band and
  multi-instrument light-curve fitting through filter transmission curves with
  MCMC, grid and nested-sampling posteriors, and physical jet models with
  afterglowpy fitted to optical, X-ray and radio data,
  and tests the fitted temporal and spectral indices against the closure
  relations of the standard fireball model. It is validated on simulated data
  with known ground truth and applied to public ZTF images of GRB 221009A and GRB 210204A.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - gamma-ray bursts
  - afterglows
  - photometry
  - image subtraction
  - PSF photometry
  - light curves
  - closure relations
  - Zwicky Transient Facility
  - nested sampling
  - Swift XRT
